      "side": 1,
      "message": "@suvedhab@ami.com, addressed this. This is handled in collectSingleFruVpd. An empty variant from the primary parse is no longer treated as a failure.\n\n1. A primary parse that throws is recorded as \"primary present but failed\". Only that case logs the primary PEL up front.\n\n2. An empty variant returned without an exception takes the separate else if (holds_alternative\u003cstd::monostate\u003e) branch. That branch calls l_collectFromRedundant(false, ...), so no primary PEL is logged at that point.\n\n3. If no redundant EEPROM is configured, the helper returns false. The caller then takes the \"both absent\" path . It sets l_fruPresenceState \u003d false and returns without throwing.",
