      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we check for std::monostate after parsing the redundant EEPROM? If its file is missing and no pre-action is required, parseVpdFile() returns an empty variant without throwing. This helper then returns success, so the caller logs a successful redundant collection and eventually marks it Completed, although no VPD was collected.",
