      "writtenOn": "2026-11-24T04:57:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that collectFromRedundantEeprom returns true when parseVpdFile() gives back an empty variant. That is documented in the header: \"check o_parsedVpd to know if the EEPROM was absent\". The check lives in the caller, not the helper.\n\nAt worker.cpp:1593-1594, the caller tests `l_parsedVpd` before it logs success.\n\nPrimary present but failed: it throws FirmwareException (\"No usable redundant EEPROM found\"). The success log is never reached, and the outer catch marks the collection Failed.\nPrimary absent: it treats the FRU as absent (l_fruPresenceState \u003d false) and returns without error.\nThe \"VPD collected from redundant EEPROM\" log and the primary PEL (worker.cpp:1609-1617) only run when `l_parsedVpd` holds real data.",
